    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i tried drying it out with some towels but the error just keeps coming back after a few cycles. it feels like there's still water sitting in that little tray at the very bottom that i can't reach. is there a specific way to get into that base pan to make sure it's completely dry?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the error keeps returning, that stubborn water in the base pan is likely the problem, and it's probably not just a simple puddle. You'll need to look for a drain or access point on the underside of the dishwasher, which is often where the sump or drain pump area is located. Sometimes, you can gently tilt the machine or use a wet/dry vacuum with a long hose attachment to try and pull out any standing water from those hard-to-reach crevices. If you can't locate an obvious drain, you might need to carefully remove the kick panel at the front to get a better view of the internal components.",
